// .groovy.jar.ae — the Apache Groovy RUNTIME jar, pinned by sha256.
//
// Needed at TEST-RUN time, not compile time: `groovyc` comes from the system
// Groovy install and compiles fine without this, but every class it emits
// implements `groovy.lang.GroovyObject`. Without the runtime on the JUnit
// classpath the test class cannot load — and JUnit's classpath scanner
// silently SKIPS classes it can't load, so the suite reported
// "0 tests found" (and then failed on --fail-if-no-tests) rather than saying
// anything about Groovy. That cost real diagnosis time; see groovy/.tests.ae.
//
// Version must track the `groovyc` that compiled the classes — 5.1.0 here.
// Same committed-lockfile shape as libs/java/clojure: coordinate + content
// hash, no jar bytes; mvn_repo resolves from the cache, ~/.m2 or Central and
// verifies the sha256 fail-closed before use.
import bldr
import java
import java (central, pinned)

aeb(cap) {
    bldr.build() {
        java.mvn_repo() {
            central()
            pinned("org.apache.groovy:groovy:5.1.0", "70d972d074583cef329016e062c8839d90b73741c88fc97a3dd4710dbacc161e")
        }
    }
}
